{
  "description": "Validation cases shared by the Python package and the fpr-ff1 Rust crate (plan 00009 STEP-08). Both suites run every case and require the same outcome: 'accepted', or rejection with the named Python exception class and exactly this message. The Rust crate maps each class to one ErrorKind (FF1Error, the base class, to AlphabetRequired). A case may not be added to one suite alone; a case only one language can express carries python_only with the reason. The key is bytes(range(key_len)); tweak_hex defaults to empty; a call's missing tweak_hex means the instance's default tweak.",
  "cases": [
